WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.789 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
RoboDemo. Reconciling demonstration

2
00:00:02.789 --> 00:00:04.809 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
intent and execution progress

3
00:00:04.809 --> 00:00:06.899 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
for long-horizon manipulation.

4
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.759 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
A human demonstration shows a procedure,

5
00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:12.083 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
not just a final goal.

6
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.512 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
The reference shows what should happen.

7
00:00:17.512 --> 00:00:19.204 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
It cannot tell us what the robot

8
00:00:19.204 --> 00:00:20.421 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
has actually completed.

9
00:00:20.821 --> 00:00:22.984 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
We preserve the procedure in one memory,

10
00:00:22.984 --> 00:00:25.365 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
and track completed interactions in another.

11
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.211 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Hierarchical sampling combines sparse global

12
00:00:31.211 --> 00:00:33.847 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
and event frames with a dense motion clip.

13
00:00:34.247 --> 00:00:36.772 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Frozen semantic and motion encoders

14
00:00:36.772 --> 00:00:38.792 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
produce fused memory tokens.

15
00:00:38.792 --> 00:00:42.183 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
These write Retrieval TTT once, before rollout.

16
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.042 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
The execution branch encodes the new image,

17
00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:49.333 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
conditioned on the current robot state

18
00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:51.383 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
and the preceding executed action.

19
00:00:51.783 --> 00:00:53.747 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
It updates progress memory causally,

20
00:00:53.747 --> 00:00:55.602 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
without overwriting the reference.

21
00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.724 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Context tokens write to fast weights.

22
00:01:00.724 --> 00:01:02.567 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Action-side queries read them.

23
00:01:02.967 --> 00:01:04.616 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Inside each action block,

24
00:01:04.616 --> 00:01:07.452 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
the expert reads intent first, then refines

25
00:01:07.452 --> 00:01:10.157 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
that representation with actual progress.

26
00:01:10.557 --> 00:01:11.963 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Both memory states remain

27
00:01:11.963 --> 00:01:13.650 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
fixed during action denoising.

28
00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.527 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
When a human video is unavailable,

29
00:01:18.527 --> 00:01:20.726 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Refreward ranks robot demonstrations

30
00:01:20.726 --> 00:01:23.170 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
using the instruction and initial image.

31
00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.106 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
The selected video enters

32
00:01:25.106 --> 00:01:27.133 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
the same intent-memory interface.

33
00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:30.245 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
We first evaluate in simulation.

34
00:01:30.245 --> 00:01:33.285 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Across fifty tasks and two thousand episodes,

35
00:01:33.285 --> 00:01:35.244 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
RoboDemo achieves eighty-four

36
00:01:35.244 --> 00:01:37.001 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
point six percent success.

37
00:01:37.401 --> 00:01:39.060 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
The table shows the overall

38
00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.473 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
and level-wise results.

39
00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.743 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Across C15, C30, and C45, mean Seen-task

40
00:01:44.743 --> 00:01:47.871 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
success is ninety point seven percent.

41
00:01:48.271 --> 00:01:50.490 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
The robot-reference variant reaches

42
00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.328 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
ninety percent on Seen tasks.

43
00:01:52.328 --> 00:01:54.799 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Unseen results are reported separately.

44
00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.473 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
On C15 Seen tasks, mixing both contexts in

45
00:02:00.473 --> 00:02:03.423 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
one memory reaches seventy-three percent.

46
00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.108 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Separate memories with cascaded reads

47
00:02:06.108 --> 00:02:08.393 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
reach eighty-nine point five percent,

48
00:02:08.393 --> 00:02:09.690 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
above parallel reads.

49
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.711 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
These polygons compare the methods

50
00:02:12.711 --> 00:02:14.469 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
across nine operation groups.

51
00:02:14.869 --> 00:02:17.234 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
The left chart normalizes each group

52
00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:19.928 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
to its best method. The right chart shows

53
00:02:19.928 --> 00:02:22.359 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
actual success rates. All values come

54
00:02:22.359 --> 00:02:24.725 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
from the complete Full50 evaluation.

55
00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.041 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
The qualitative examples pair the human

56
00:02:29.041 --> 00:02:31.739 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
reference with its recorded robot execution.

57
00:02:31.739 --> 00:02:33.455 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
First, pouring between cups.

58
00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:38.944 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
The same architecture also transfers

59
00:02:38.944 --> 00:02:41.749 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
the demonstrated procedure to hanging a mug.

60
00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.083 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Folding and stowing requires multiple

61
00:02:49.083 --> 00:02:51.450 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
manipulation stages within one task.

62
00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.429 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Finally, RoboDemo achieves seventy-three

63
00:02:59.429 --> 00:03:02.138 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
point three percent mean success across

64
00:03:02.138 --> 00:03:04.778 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
three household tasks on AgiBot G two.

65
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.252 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Tabletop organization:

66
00:03:07.252 --> 00:03:10.187 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
moving objects to their intended locations.

67
00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.388 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Sofa cushion arrangement:

68
00:03:17.388 --> 00:03:20.401 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
grasping and repositioning deformable objects.

69
00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:26.975 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Bottle-to-cup pouring:

70
00:03:26.975 --> 00:03:29.313 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
coordinating the bottle and receiving cup.

71
00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:38.088 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
We also test visual changes without

72
00:03:38.088 --> 00:03:40.026 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
target-condition fine-tuning.

73
00:03:40.026 --> 00:03:41.830 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Here, the lighting changes.

74
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.981 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
Here, the tabletop background changes

75
00:03:47.981 --> 00:03:49.910 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
while the task remains the same.

76
00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.087 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
An additional recording shows tabletop

77
00:03:58.087 --> 00:03:59.931 line:-2 position:50% align:center size:88%
